From: GitHub Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: pass ARMv7 FPU flags to ffmpeg on Linux armhf

FFmpeg's Linux/arm configure path emits `-march=armv7-a` but no matching
`-mfpu=...` flag. On Debian's hard-float cross toolchain that makes the
compiler self-test fail with:

  cc1: error: '-mfloat-abi=hard': selected architecture lacks an FPU

Plumb an explicit VFPv3-D16 target flag into ffmpeg's extra C flags for the
Linux ARMv7 contrib build so the hard-float compiler test can succeed.
This stays scoped to Linux armv7 and does not affect host tools or other
platforms.
---
 contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak b/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
index 0fe31de..75706f8 100644
--- a/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
@@ -109,6 +109,11 @@ endif
 # ARM stuff
 ifeq ($(ARCH),arm)
 FFMPEGCONF += --arch=arm
+ifdef HAVE_LINUX
+ifdef HAVE_ARMV7A
+FFMPEGCONF += --extra-cflags="$(CFLAGS) -mfpu=vfpv3-d16"
+endif
+endif
 ifdef HAVE_NEON
 FFMPEGCONF += --enable-neon
 endif
